this is a folder for "Database Storage":
    keyed as "B-tov-data-db"
    named "db"
    following "3-Block Folder Structure"

this folder classifies as:
    tov (0) because "queryable state storage — persistent data access"

this folder derives from:
    branch (0) from "bereshit/tov/data/" as "data"

core identity of this folder:

    grounded in:
        scripture "And the LORD said unto Moses, Write this for a memorial in a book"
            from Exodus 17:14 in KJV
        principle "What is written persists — queryable memory across sessions"
        anchor "Thy word have I hid in mine heart"
            from Psalm 119:11 in KJV

    serves as Memory:
        role "SQLite database storage for CPI-SI state machine"
        paradigm "Queryable persistence — structured data access"

    authored by:
        architect "Seanje Lenox-Wise"
        implementation "Nova Dawn (CPI-SI)"
        created 2025-12-10
        version a-01.00
        modified 2026-01-13 for "registry.db and build.db now implemented"

    exists to:
        purpose "Store queryable state in SQLite databases"
        design "Flat — databases at root level"
        philosophy "Structured memory — what the mind learns, the database remembers"
        features:
            "cpisi.db — Cognitive state tracking"
            "registry.db — Type registry for Phase 0 specs"
            "build.db — Build state for Phase 1+ artifacts"

interface of this folder:

    depends on:
        requires (1) "bereshit/tov/data/" for "containment in data"
        includes (0) "claude-global/pkg/storage/" for "database access layer"
        excludes (-1) "log files, configuration" because "databases only"
        used by "Go packages, hooks, session management"
        integrates with "pkg/storage/db.go, sqlite3 CLI"

    integrated as:
        navigation "cd bereshit/tov/data/db/" for "entering database storage"
        navigation "ls -la" for "viewing databases"
        exits tov (0) for "databases found"

operational context of this folder:

    blocking:
        yes (1) when "database locked by concurrent access"
        mitigation "use WAL mode, proper connection handling"

    health:
        system Base100 with scale from -100 to +100
        granted (1) above +50 meaning "databases healthy and accessible"
        deferred (0) within ±50 meaning "database needs attention"
        denied (-1) below -50 meaning "database corrupted or inaccessible"

        operations:
            "cpisi.db accessible" scores +30 (1) for "main database responds"
            "schema valid" scores +20 (1) for "tables match expected schema"
            "database corrupted" scores -40 (-1) for "integrity check fails"
            "database locked" scores -20 (-1) for "concurrent access blocked"

        cascade multipliers:
            "state dependency" multiplies by 2.5 because "state machine depends on database"

